import hashlib,json,pathlib
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_pfp_infrastructure_remaining';f=json.loads((H/(P+'_preparation.json')).read_text())['files'];rp=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(rp.read_text())
def ev(i,a,b):return {'path':f[i]['path'],'sha256':f[i]['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
rows=[
('051','Canonical SQLite example uses incompatible PostgreSQL syntax','The relational template labels its canonical example sqlite_strict_text_set_v1, but all three INSERTs use PostgreSQL ::text casts. The exact first fixed INSERT fails in an in-memory SQLite database with an unrecognized-colon error. Double-quoted SQL strings and backslash escaping also require correction for portable SQLite literals.',[ev(527,95,107)],['059'],'Generate canonical examples using the declared SQL dialect and run a bounded parse/roundtrip check.'),
('052','Representation examples and symbolic regex disagree with declared grammar','The symbolic wire regex includes a literal space in [qcdo u], accepting a forbidden role character. Cochain/diagram/egraph/operadic canonical source IDs contain colons excluded by their own declared source_id regex. These files use descriptive specification.fields, not directly executable JSON Schema.',[ev(529,24,67),ev(522,1,131),ev(523,1,160),ev(524,1,117),ev(525,155,179)],['060','061'],'Remove the accidental regex space and align examples with the intended source-ID language; validate with actual representation parsers, not metadata alone.'),
('053','Operadic example grafts refer to undeclared producer instances','Only verify_substitution is declared as an operator, but root grafts reference verify_substitution_eq1 and verify_substitution_eq2 without an instance-to-operator map or their inputs. Other producer subtrees are not supplied. This is an architectural sketch rather than a complete executable typed grafting tree or verified operad law table.',[ev(535,87,119)],[],'Declare typed operation instances with all inputs/outputs, then validate the complete finite tree; keep associativity/unit/equivariance laws distinct from one wiring example.'),
('054','Illustrative rational deltoid cusps lie off the stated curve','Compressed template gives(-3/2,+/-21/8) as cusps. Substitution into the related operadic deltoid polynomial yields81/4096 rather than0. Exact-looking rational coordinates cannot serve as exact boundary/cusp evidence.',[ev(536,108,138),ev(525,155,165)],['062'],'Correct the illustrative carrier/coordinates or explicitly label approximations and certified enclosures; do not silently repair historical bytes.'),
('055','Planned digest-separation theorem upgrades collision resistance to injectivity','The proposed Lean statement requires different arbitrary LossLedgers to have different SHA256 digests. Any admissible ledger domain with more than2^256 values violates that statement by pigeonhole. Computational collision resistance is not universal injectivity.',[ev(504,178,181)],['065'],'State the computational threat model and collision assumption, or restrict to an exhaustively proven finite domain. Treat this roadmap as planned obligations, not existing proved tests.'),
('056','Planned supersymmetry test combines incompatible nonzero-Hamiltonian conditions','The roadmap simultaneously requires{Qi,Qj}=2delta_ij H and Q1²=Q2²=0. For i=j in characteristic0 this forces H=0. Real supercharges squaring toH and complex nilpotent combinations have been conflated.',[ev(504,615,618)],['064'],'Specify the supercharge convention and correct conjugate anticommutators before implementing tests. No existing native test failure is claimed.'),
('057','Acyclic marginal gluing is incorrectly claimed unique','The roadmap promises unique global distribution from compatible marginals on an acyclic cover. Uniform independent binary A,B,C and a distribution with A=C and independent fair B have identical uniform AB and BC marginals but differ globally. Ordinary point-valued sheaf gluing and probabilistic marginal extension must be distinguished.',[ev(504,727,734),ev(58,1,1)],['063'],'Claim existence under the necessary compatibility hypotheses; add conditional-independence or another specified selection principle for a chosen extension, not arbitrary uniqueness.'),
('058','Pilot receipt schemas permit absent evidence and negative accounting','Comparison schema accepts{}; response schema accepts COMPLETED/ACCEPTED without raw_reply and with empty receipt. Negative provider_calls/cost/tokens and inconsistent total_tokens also validate. These exported schemas cannot by themselves enforce the raw-custody/cryptographic-spend claims in their descriptions.',[ev(508,143,175),ev(509,118,146),ev(509,169,264)],['066'],'Require appropriate fields conditionally on execution state and impose nonnegative accounting/binding invariants. Keep actual domain validators separate; this probe does not allege their runtime acceptance.'),
('059','Stage schema fixed annotations do not enforce mandatory safety values','A stage5 record validates with preserve_original_seed=false, retain_stage_2_candidates=false, independent_checker_required=false and candidate_source_stage=99. x-slot fixed only annotates fields; Boolean presence does not require true. Nullable response schemas and controller population also need host checks.',[ev(578,39,60),ev(578,233,257)],['067'],'Encode constants/source-stage bounds where mandatory and validate complete controller population at admission, alongside runtime behavior.'),
('060','Data-type catalog still specifies eight stages against the eleven-stage controller','PfpStageFile caps stage at8 and controller description/default remain8, while current generated stage schema and controller define11. The broader catalog also retains older framing/NF/checker vocabulary; it is not a reliable replacement for dedicated current schemas.',[ev(505,1659,1668),ev(505,1712,1726),ev(566,1,145),ev(578,1,38)],[],'Regenerate and compare authoritative type/schema/controller definitions; distinguish intentional historical editions from current admission contracts.'),
('061','Three Q40 Pauli fixture descriptions misstate commutation','Exact Pauli parity census finds6 anticommuting pairs in q40_07 described as a stabilizer ring,60 in q40_18 described as exactly24 commuting terms, and zero in q40_23 described as noncommuting stabilizers. All40 carriers have valid word lengths/alphabet,positive rational weights and target signs; this is semantic labeling drift, not malformed encoding.',[ev(30,131,160),ev(30,430,555),ev(30,640,665)],['068'],'Correct labels or Hamiltonian terms and bind benchmark grouping to computed properties. Do not interpret mislabeled group outcomes as tests of the advertised mathematical family.'),
('062','Generated discovery catalogs retain stale current-checkout pins','All101 packaged checker/fixture/row pins and clause controls agree, but the broader scenario catalog has one stale cohomology fixture digest and14 absent declared implementation paths. The744-entry operad catalog has correct kind counts/arity/source declarations but only9 of52 pinned sources match current bytes;8 differ and35 historical paths are absent. This limits replay against the current checkout.',[ev(1,445,457),ev(20,1,1),ev(519,1,29),ev(519,9335,9545)],[],'Retain historical catalogs and source revisions; publish a separately pinned relocation/current-edition mapping with validated sources. Missing old relative paths do not establish original evidence loss, and the catalog explicitly denies theorem/authority/efficacy claims.'),
]
